From cdb5fb46407ffd6a5ce7231fbb950a1991d85957 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kob <kob@invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:43:05 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Priority levels: ask the next level only after every provider
 missed

Client::request walked every provider on any failure, so a primary that was
down, stalled, saturated, breaker-open or withdrawn a request sent the article to
backup and block accounts. A level now ends the request unless every provider on
it missed (430, corrupt copy, past retention); failures and skips end it with
the provider error or Unavailable. Upstream tests that relied on cross-level
failover after a failure now place the providers on one level.
